      source: "Portrait of Kobo Daishi (Kukai), hanging scroll in ink, colors and gold on silk, artist unknown, Japanese, 14th century, Art Institute of Chicago, reference number 1960.40, gift of Robert Allerton. The museum's own object page carries a CC0 Public Domain Designation and its API lists the work as public domain with no copyright notice; the work is roughly 700 years old. A devotional portrait painted some five centuries after his death, so shown as a later depiction and not as a likeness. The photograph shows the whole mounted scroll. Original image 3623 x 5440 pixels from the museum's IIIF server, downscaled to 799 x 1200 with no cropping and no upscaling.",
