      cross_domain_range: [62, 0.46, "s", "A"],
      // [src_kukai_nwe, src_kukai_eb, src_kukai_bowker | 806-835 | edited encyclopedia + scholarly reference + dictionary] After his return he sent the court a catalogue of what he had brought and a petition for support in 809, petitioned in 810 to perform certain rituals, and in 834 petitioned for a Shingon chapel in the palace, which was granted and put Shingon ritual into the court calendar; the grants of Mount Koya in 816 and Toji in 823 are given by the dictionary and the temple as the centres of the school. The petitions are reported by one edited encyclopedia and the outline is shared with the reference entries, so the row is moderate and does not score the court relationship itself.
