      impact_motivation: [70, 0.55, "s", "A"],
      // [src_nawal_isu, src_nawal_olympedia | 1977-1987 | university biography + Olympic statistics biography] ISU says she was a reluctant hurdler ranked 26th in the world in 1983, returned to form for Los Angeles after an ankle injury curtailed her post-collegiate season, and kept winning afterwards (four Big Eight titles, an NCAA title, two Mediterranean Games golds); Olympedia lists African, Mediterranean and Universiade titles between 1982 and 1987. These show sustained competing and a documented comeback, but the sources do not describe her own effort in detail.
